{"data": {"notes": [], "reqs": [{"kind": "contract", "priority": "hard", "requirement_id": "R1", "source": {"type": "task_metadata"}, "status": "active", "text": "Entry point `solve` in language python, within the stated limits.", "version": 1}, {"kind": "explicit", "priority": "hard", "requirement_id": "R2", "source": {"char_end": 1524, "char_start": 0, "quote": "You are an expert Python programmer. You will be given a question (problem specification) and will generate a correct Python program that matches the specification and passes all tests.\n\n### Question:\nYou are given an integer sequence A=(A_1,A_2,A_3,A_4,A_5) obtained by permuting (1,2,3,4,5).\nDetermine whether A can be sorted in ascending order by performing exactly one operation of swapping two adjacent elements in A.\n\nInput\n\nThe input is given from Standard Input in the following format:\nA_1 A_2 A_3 A_4 A_5\n\nOutput\n\nIf A can be sorted in ascending order by exactly one operation, print Yes; otherwise, print No.\n\nConstraints\n\n\n- A is an integer sequence of length 5 obtained by permuting (1,2,3,4,5).\n\nSample Input 1\n\n1 2 4 3 5\n\nSample Output 1\n\nYes\r\n\nBy swapping A_3 and A_4, A becomes (1,2,3,4,5), so it can be sorted in ascending order. Therefore, print Yes.\n\nSample Input 2\n\n5 3 2 4 1\n\nSample Output 2\n\nNo\r\n\nNo matter what operation is performed, it is impossible to sort A in ascending order.\n\nSample Input 3\n\n1 2 3 4 5\n\nSample Output 3\n\nNo\r\n\nYou must perform exactly one operation.\n\nSample Input 4\n\n2 1 3 4 5\n\nSample Output 4\n\nYes\n\n### Format: Read the inputs from stdin solve the problem and write the answer to stdout (do not directly test on the sample inputs). Enclose your code within delimiters as follows. Ensure that when the python program runs, it reads the inputs, runs the algorithm and writes output to STDOUT.\n```python\n# YOUR CODE HERE\n```\n\n### Answer: (use the provided format with backticks)\n\n", "type": "request_span"}, "status": "active", "text": "The program is correct on all legal inputs of the statement.", "version": 1}, {"kind": "explicit", "priority": "functional", "requirement_id": "R3", "source": {"char_end": 1564, "char_start": 1536, "quote": "Input:\n1 2 4 3 5\nOutput:\nYes", "type": "request_span"}, "status": "active", "text": "Public example 1: output exactly the quoted output for the quoted input.", "version": 1}, {"kind": "explicit", "priority": "functional", "requirement_id": "R4", "source": {"char_end": 1603, "char_start": 1576, "quote": "Input:\n5 3 2 4 1\nOutput:\nNo", "type": "request_span"}, "status": "active", "text": "Public example 2: output exactly the quoted output for the quoted input.", "version": 1}, {"kind": "explicit", "priority": "functional", "requirement_id": "R5", "source": {"char_end": 1642, "char_start": 1615, "quote": "Input:\n1 2 3 4 5\nOutput:\nNo", "type": "request_span"}, "status": "active", "text": "Public example 3: output exactly the quoted output for the quoted input.", "version": 1}, {"kind": "explicit", "priority": "functional", "requirement_id": "R6", "source": {"char_end": 1682, "char_start": 1654, "quote": "Input:\n2 1 3 4 5\nOutput:\nYes", "type": "request_span"}, "status": "active", "text": "Public example 4: output exactly the quoted output for the quoted input.", "version": 1}], "request_sha": "a6db6df42fceba1653c7d4f2ca8b448d650d4417b18c81a0349edac26d3d3903", "stop": null}, "kind": "requirements", "prev": "cfa67519d104a3e5b7a08b153ea3410fe50e79b60aee984732c92a0f6c5cac71", "seq": 2}
